# Bill of Materials (BOM) - Greenhouse Link 🌿🍄

This document lists all physical components, electronic modules, and hardware required to build the Greenhouse Link control box and remote sensor units.

---

## 1. Modules, Electronics & Control
* **1x** ESP32 DevKit V1 (30 pins or more)
* **1x** Relay Module Setup (Totaling **12 channels** of 3V3/5V relay modules, including a separate standalone relay module dedicated to the soil moisture sensor control circuit)
* **1x** Power Supply 5V / >2A (or DC-DC Buck Converter for other setups)

## 2. Remote Sensors & Signal Conditioning
* **1x** Soil Moisture Sensor - optional (Capacitive v1.2 or better recommended, need the standalone relay module here)
* **1x** Air Temperature & Humidity / Gas Sensor (SCD30 for CO₂ or DHT11/DHT22 for basic setup)
* **2x** Resistors (4.7 k$\Omega$ / 4k7)
* **1x** Electrolytic Capacitor (100 µF)

## 3. Connectivity & Cabling (RJ45 Standard)
* **Cables:** UTP Cat5e or Cat6 Ethernet Cable (recommended bright color for greenhouse identification)
* **Panel Connectors:** **2x** RJ45 Female Panel Mount Connectors
* **Internal Wiring:** Dupont jumper wires (male/female) and perfboard/protoboard

## 4. Enclosures, Fastening & Hardware
* **Enclosures:**
  * **1x** Main big ABS Waterproof Junction Box (for ESP32, relays, and power supply - around 20x20cm)
  * **1x** Remote small ABS Junction Box (for soil and air sensors - outlet standard size)
* **Fasteners:**
  * **M2 Screw Kit:** M2 screws, M2x10mm standoffs (spacers), and nuts for secure module mounting inside the enclosures
* **Finishing & Organization:**
  * **Cable ties (Zip ties):** For strain relief on RJ45 cables
  * **Heat shrink tubing:** For soldered connection insulation

